The fix adds a check for `ITER_KVEC` in `netfs_limit_iter()`, directing it to the new `netfs_limit_kvec()` function. This function follows the same pattern as `netfs_limit_bvec()`, correctly handling the segment array of an `ITER_KVEC` iterator by walking its `kvec` array and applying the size and segment limits. This prevents the `BUG()` from being triggered when `ITER_KVEC` iterators are used, such as during core dump writes.

